# Use uv for Everything Python

Never use `pip`, `pip install`, `python -m venv`, `poetry`, or `conda` directly.

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Add a dependency | `uv add <package>` |
| Add a dev dependency | `uv add --dev <package>` |
| Remove a dependency | `uv remove <package>` |
| Install / sync the environment | `uv sync` |
| Run a script | `uv run main.py` |
| Run a tool (pytest, ruff, etc.) | `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check .` |
| One-off tool without installing | `uvx <tool>` |
| Upgrade the lockfile | `uv lock --upgrade` |

- Dependencies live in `pyproject.toml`; never create `requirements.txt` unless explicitly asked.
- Commit `uv.lock`; never edit it by hand.
- Respect the version in `.python-version`; use `uv python pin <version>` to change it.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
pip install svgpathtools
python main.py

# ✅ GOOD
uv add svgpathtools
uv run main.py
```
